-- Regression pins for the deontic breach-semantics fix cluster:
--
--   (b) RAND/ROR over ANY both-breached pair (DeadlineMissed and/or
--       ExplicitBreach) reports a breach instead of a residual, ANCHORED at
--       one operand (RAND the earliest, ROR the latest; untimestamped pairs
--       tie-break RAND left, ROR right), naming BOTH failures with their detail.
--   (c) the event whose timestamp reveals deadline expiry is re-offered to
--       the HENCE/LEST continuation instead of being silently consumed;
--       a LEST continuation's clock starts at the MISSED DEADLINE
--       (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.2, since 2026-09-16), so the
--       re-offered event may already lie past the continuation's own
--       deadline.
--   (d) the deadline boundary is strict: arriving exactly AT the deadline is
--       timely; a violated prohibition reuses the event stamp as its
--       "deadline" sentinel.
--   (e) a literal pinned in per-argument position (the corrected README
--       example; it was written MUST pay EXACTLY 100 until R1 retired the
--       keyword, and a literal in pattern position always meant this).
--   (f) recursive LEST with a non-positive computed WITHIN terminates:
--       the deadline-revealing event is re-offered AT MOST ONCE.
--   MAY expiry routes to LEST (default FULFILLED) per the README
--   default-consequence matrix; HENCE fires only on exercise. The HENCE
--   and LEST continuations here differ in party AND action so the golden
--   output distinguishes which branch fired.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
  deliver
  smoke
  exercise

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (b) both alternatives breached
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`ror both explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed first")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "missed second")

-- Both alternatives definitively breached => single breach (not a residual OR),
-- naming BOTH failures, left first, each with its own BECAUSE.
#TRACE `ror both explicit` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`rand both explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed first")
    RAND
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "missed second")

-- RAND over an untimestamped pair: both failures, each with its own BECAUSE.
#TRACE `rand both explicit` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`explicit or deadline` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`deadline or explicit` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)
    ROR
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")

-- Mixed kinds, both orders: anchored at the RIGHT operand's breach, naming BOTH.
#TRACE `explicit or deadline` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `deadline or explicit` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one breached one pending` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "missed payment")
    ROR
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Control: only ONE alternative breached, the other still live => residual
-- (Bob may still deliver); the compound must NOT breach yet.
#TRACE `one breached one pending` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 7)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (c) the deadline-revealing event is re-offered to the continuation
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`late delivery discharges the reparation` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 100
  WITHIN 5
  LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Bob's delivery AT 7 both reveals Alice's expiry (7 > 5) AND is the very
-- action the LEST reparation waits for => FULFILLED (not a pending residual).
#TRACE `late delivery discharges the reparation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

`prohibition hence sees the revealer` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 5
  HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

-- Same re-offer on the prohibition HENCE path: the prohibition was respected,
-- and the revealing delivery discharges the HENCE obligation => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `prohibition hence sees the revealer` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

`anchor at the deadline` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 2
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3)

-- The continuation's clock anchors at the missed deadline (2), so its own
-- deadline is 5. The re-offered event (Bob at 7, wrong party) is already
-- past it: it reveals a second expiry, is consumed rather than re-offered
-- again, and — the LEST having no LEST of its own — the answer is a breach
-- dated 7 with deadline 5. (Until 2026-09-16 the clock anchored at the
-- revealing stamp, 7, the re-offered event decremented the WITHIN by zero
-- and the residual read WITHIN 3.)
#TRACE `anchor at the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7

`nested peel` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 2
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))

-- Each re-offer peels exactly one HENCE/LEST layer (termination). WAIT@20
-- expires layer 1 (deadline 2) and is re-offered to layer 2, which counts
-- from 2 and is due at 5 — so the same WAIT@20, now marked, reveals a
-- second expiry and is CONSUMED; layer 3 counts from 5 and is due at 15.
-- WAIT@30 expires it: no LEST, so a breach dated 30 with deadline 15, and
-- Bob's delivery at 35 is never reached. (Until 2026-09-16 each layer
-- counted from the revealing stamp — deadlines 2, 23, 40 — and the
-- delivery at 35 discharged layer 3: FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `nested peel` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 30)
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 35

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`one event repairs both alternatives` MEANS
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 2 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))
    ROR
    (PARTY Alice MUST pay 2 WITHIN 3 LEST (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10))

-- Re-offer x ROR interaction: the single late delivery reveals expiry on BOTH
-- alternatives and is then re-offered inside each, fulfilling both LESTs.
#TRACE `one event repairs both alternatives` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (d) at-deadline boundary; SHANT stamp-as-deadline sentinel
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`pay due` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 100
  WITHIN 5

-- Exactly AT the deadline: timely.
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 100 AT 5

-- Clock advanced exactly TO the deadline: not yet expired (residual WITHIN 0).
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

-- Strictly past the deadline: breach, "deadline, which was at 5".
#TRACE `pay due` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 6)

`no smoking` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  SHANT smoke
  WITHIN 30

-- Prohibited action exactly AT the deadline is still a violation; the breach
-- record reuses the event stamp as its "deadline" sentinel (both fields 30).
#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES smoke AT 30

-- Prohibition respected once the deadline has passed => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (e) a literal pinned in per-argument position (corrected README example)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`pay exactly 100` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 100
  WITHIN 30

#TRACE `pay exactly 100` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 100 AT 10

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- MAY expiry routes to LEST; HENCE fires only on exercise
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- HENCE (Bob delivers) and LEST (Alice pays 50) are deliberately
-- DISTINGUISHABLE — different party and action — so these traces pin the
-- ROUTING, not just the outcome: were expiry mis-routed to HENCE, the first
-- trace would leave Bob's delivery obligation as a residual instead of
-- FULFILLED.
`may with lest` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MAY exercise
  WITHIN 5
  HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)
  LEST (PARTY Alice MUST pay 50 WITHIN 20)

-- Permission NOT exercised: expiry routes to LEST (Alice's reparation
-- payment), and the revealing payment is re-offered to it => FULFILLED.
#TRACE `may with lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 50 AT 7

-- Permission exercised: the HENCE obligation (Bob delivers) becomes the
-- residual.
#TRACE `may with lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES exercise AT 3

`may bare` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MAY exercise
  WITHIN 5

-- Bare MAY expiry: LEST defaults to FULFILLED (same outcome as before).
#TRACE `may bare` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 9)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- (f) recursive LEST with a non-positive WITHIN terminates
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`recursive lest` MEANS
  PARTY Alice
  MUST pay 1
  WITHIN 0 - 1
  LEST `recursive lest`

-- The LEST recursively re-invokes the same obligation, whose computed WITHIN
-- is negative, so each incarnation's deadline is already past at its own
-- anchor (the previous incarnation's missed deadline: -1, then -2). The
-- revealing event (Bob's delivery — wrong party, wrong action) is
-- re-offered ONCE to the first LEST incarnation; when it reveals a second
-- expiry there, it is consumed instead of being re-offered again, so
-- evaluation terminates with the recursive obligation as the residual
-- (before the at-most-once rule this trace looped forever).
#TRACE `recursive lest` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7
